.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-cert-issuer 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-cert\-issuer \- Issues a delegation issuer pair: `issuer.<name>.crt` and `issuer.<name>.key`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring cert issuer\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-name\fR> <\fB\-\-dir\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Issues a delegation issuer pair: `issuer.<name>.crt` and `issuer.<name>.key`
.PP
The control node signs delegated agents\*(Aq tokens with the key, and they carry the certificate. Each run makes a new key; name the files in the control node\*(Aqs `[control] issuer_cert` and `issuer_key`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The issuer\*(Aqs name: by convention, the control node\*(Aqs ID
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The directory with `ca.crt` and `ca.key`

The new files go into it unless `\-\-out` names another.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Writes the files into this directory instead, created private to you
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR
How long the certificate lasts: `<n>d`, `<n>h`, `<n>m`, or `<n>s`

30 days by default, and at most 90.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
